        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Evaluate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow -3}\\dfrac{x^2-9}{x+3}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Evaluate [MATH: \\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow -3}\\dfrac{x^2-9}{x+3}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow -3}\\dfrac{x^2-9}{x+3} = \\dfrac{(-3)^2-9}{(-3)+3} = \\dfrac{0}{0}\n}]</span></p><p>So, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: (x^{2} \u2212 9)/(x + 3)|= (x^{2} \u2212 3^{2})/(x + 3); = ((x + 3)(x \u2212 3))/(x + 3); = (x \u2212 3).]</span></p><p>Therefore,\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: lim_(x \u2192 \u2212 3)(x^{2} \u2212 9)/(x + 3)|= lim_(x \u2192 \u2212 3)(x \u2212 3); = \u2212 3 \u2212 3; = \u2212 6.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow -3}\\dfrac{x^2-9}{x+3} = \\dfrac{(-3)^2-9}{(-3)+3} = \\dfrac{0}{0}\n}]\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n[MATH: (x^{2} \u2212 9)/(x + 3)|= (x^{2} \u2212 3^{2})/(x + 3); = ((x + 3)(x \u2212 3))/(x + 3); = (x \u2212 3).]\n\nTherefore,\n[MATH: lim_(x \u2192 \u2212 3)(x^{2} \u2212 9)/(x + 3)|= lim_(x \u2192 \u2212 3)(x \u2212 3); = \u2212 3 \u2212 3; = \u2212 6.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: \\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow -3}\\dfrac{x^2-9}{x+3}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nIf we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow -3}\\dfrac{x^2-9}{x+3} = \\dfrac{(-3)^2-9}{(-3)+3} = \\dfrac{0}{0}\n}]\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n[MATH: (x^{2} \u2212 9)/(x + 3)|= (x^{2} \u2212 3^{2})/(x + 3); = ((x + 3)(x \u2212 3))/(x + 3); = (x \u2212 3).]\n\nTherefore,\n[MATH: lim_(x \u2192 \u2212 3)(x^{2} \u2212 9)/(x + 3)|= lim_(x \u2192 \u2212 3)(x \u2212 3); = \u2212 3 \u2212 3; = \u2212 6.]"
      },
