          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 6}\\dfrac{x^2-6x}{x^2-x-30} = \\dfrac{6^2-6\\cdot 6}{6^2-6-30} = \\dfrac{0}{0}\n}]</span></p><p>So, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: (x^{2} \u2212 6x)/(x^{2} \u2212 x \u2212 30)|= (x(x \u2212 6))/((x \u2212 6)(x + 5)) = (x)/(x + 5).]</span></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: lim_(x \u2192 6)(x^{2} \u2212 6x)/(x^{2} \u2212 x \u2212 30)|= lim_(x \u2192 6)(x)/(x + 5); = (6)/(6 + 5); = (6)/(11).]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 6}\\dfrac{x^2-6x}{x^2-x-30} = \\dfrac{6^2-6\\cdot 6}{6^2-6-30} = \\dfrac{0}{0}\n}]\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n[MATH: (x^{2} \u2212 6x)/(x^{2} \u2212 x \u2212 30)|= (x(x \u2212 6))/((x \u2212 6)(x + 5)) = (x)/(x + 5).]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: lim_(x \u2192 6)(x^{2} \u2212 6x)/(x^{2} \u2212 x \u2212 30)|= lim_(x \u2192 6)(x)/(x + 5); = (6)/(6 + 5); = (6)/(11).]",
